  "在超過3年的新冠疫情下，社交距離措施影響人與人的交流。香港浸會大學教育學系團隊今日(18日)公布研究，結果發現有特殊需要": "In the COVID-19 epidemic that has lasted for more than three years, social distancing measures have affected communication between people. A team from the Department of Education of Hong Kong Baptist University announced a study today (18th) and found that there are special needs",
  "【📻電台節目重溫】社區探索活動設計竅妙\n\n我哋嘅服務主管李嘉萱早前聯同參與過親切大澳社區探索活動嘅能障同學、特殊學校嘅老師及義工，參與商業電台881「同途有心人」節目。社區元素對能障兒童嚟講點解咁重要？親切如何運用社區探索活動，回應到能障學童嘅成長需要？活動嘅設計上，我哋如何因應": "[📻Radio program review] Tips on designing community exploration activities\n\nOur service supervisor, Ms. Li Ka-suan, recently joined hands with disabled students who participated in TREATS Tai O community exploration activities, teachers and volunteers from special schools to participate in the program \"People with Hearts on the Same Journey\" on Commercial Radio 881. How important are community elements to children with disabilities? How does TREATS use community exploration activities to respond to the developmental needs of students with disabilities? How do we respond to the design of activities?",
