  "智障人士要運動原來不易，有智障人士的母親表示，曾為兒子報名參加康文署的乒乓班，但因教練不懂得與智障人士相處，安排其子「企埋一邊拍下個波就算": "It is not easy for people with intellectual disabilities to exercise. The mother of a person with intellectual disabilities said that she once signed up her son for a table tennis class of the Leisure and Cultural Services Department, but because the coach did not know how to get along with people with intellectual disabilities, he arranged for his son to \"bury himself in the ground while taking pictures.\"",
  "世上有項唯一可以讓三隊同時作賽的球類運動，名為「健球」。最近有機構在港引入這新興運動，還加入共融元素，讓有特殊需要學生跟商界義工一齊合作。\n\n想了解更多健球的共融理念，可參閱今日出版的《親子王》。\n\n——————\n更多精彩內容即去《親子王》\n揭頁版網頁：bit.ly/1rnzTU": "There is the only ball game in the world that allows three teams to compete at the same time, called \"Kineball\". Recently, some organizations have introduced this new movement in Hong Kong and added elements of inclusion, allowing students with special needs to work together with volunteers from the business sector.\n\nIf you want to know more about the inclusive concept of Jianqiu, you can read the \"Parent-Child King\" published today.\n\n——————\nFor more exciting content, please go to \"Parent-Child King\"\nRevealed page: bit.ly/1rnzTU",
