  "踏入尖沙咀一間咖啡店，咖啡香味撲鼻而來，患有輕度智障及自閉症的青年彭鈺林小心翼翼將熱水倒進杯內，為客人沖調飲品。約半年前，他經社工介紹參與非政府機構「親切」的青少年職場共融體驗計劃，在店內實習及兼職，性格由沉默寡言變得主動。彭媽媽是首名顧客，她回想喝兒子首杯沖泡的咖啡，每一口都甜": "Stepping into a coffee shop in Tsim Sha Tsui, the aroma of coffee fills your nostrils. Peng Yulin, a young man with mild mental retardation and autism, carefully pours hot water into a cup to prepare drinks for the customers. About six months ago, he was introduced by a social worker to participate in the youth workplace inclusion experience program of the non-governmental organization \"TREATS\". He worked as an intern and part-time job in the store, and his personality changed from reticent to active. Peng’s mother was the first customer. She recalled drinking her son’s first cup of coffee and every sip was sweet.",
